  "description": "WADQOL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C106 H91 Ce4 N7 O25 2+,2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.767-5.291 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.64-162.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C106H91Ce4N7O25·2(NO3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(III).",
